.TH dopewars 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
dopewars \- the street-trading game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dopewars
.SH DESCRIPTION
A rewrite of John Dell's Drug Wars, after the Happy Hacker Foundation
DOS version and Matthew Lee's PalmOS one.  You have 31 days to make as
much money as you can buying low and selling high around New York, with
2,000 in cash and a debt of 5,500 to the loan shark.  Prices move from
day to day and place to place, a bust sends one sky-high and a glut
makes one crash, and the police may come after you.
.PP
Each command is a letter followed by Return:
.TP
.B b
Buy.
.TP
.B s
Sell.
.TP
.B i
Show what you hold.
.TP
.B m
Move to another part of the city, which takes a day.
.TP
.B d
Done for today.
.TP
.B Q
Quit and count up.
.PP
In the Bronx, where you start, there are two more:
.B l
for the loan shark and
.B a
for the bank.
.PP
At the end your money is counted and the game says how you did.
There is no saved game.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hamurabi (1)
